{
  "id": "srgb-transfer",
  "description": "The sRGB transfer function (IEC 61966-2-1:1999). Weighted towards near-black, where the piecewise linear segment lives and where a pure-power implementation is wrong by up to a factor of 39. Entries below the cutoff have tolerance 0: the linear branch is a single IEEE-754 division, which is exactly rounded and therefore identical on every conforming runtime. Entries on the power branch carry a real tolerance, because ECMAScript specifies Math.pow as implementation-approximated.",
